00:00:27.831 --> 00:00:31.204
So Gary Vaynerchuk is known for hustle.

00:00:31.204 --> 00:00:32.145
- Okay.

00:00:32.145 --> 00:00:34.108
- So talk to me what
does hustle mean to you?

00:00:34.108 --> 00:00:35.989
Why is it important?

00:00:35.989 --> 00:00:38.665
- For me it's important because

00:00:38.665 --> 00:00:40.374
I don't think any of us in this room

00:00:40.374 --> 00:00:44.629
or anybody reading this
article can physically

00:00:44.629 --> 00:00:46.543
change how smart they are.

00:00:46.543 --> 00:00:50.693
I don't think we can make
ourselves more clever

00:00:50.693 --> 00:00:52.777
or more strategic,

00:00:52.777 --> 00:00:55.662
but I do think that hard work is the

00:00:55.662 --> 00:00:59.321
most controllable aspect of
entrepreneurship and business

00:00:59.321 --> 00:01:01.321
that anybody can deploy.

00:01:03.246 --> 00:01:04.754
And I find that fascinating.

00:01:04.754 --> 00:01:07.430
Right, it's very hard for us to be born

00:01:07.430 --> 00:01:09.106
with more physical attributes,

00:01:09.106 --> 00:01:11.560
but if we work out seven days a week

00:01:11.560 --> 00:01:14.188
we can be more athletic
we can be stronger.

00:01:14.188 --> 00:01:17.050
I think work ethic aka hustle

00:01:17.050 --> 00:01:20.749
is that same version in business it's

00:01:20.749 --> 00:01:23.084
the most controllable and I try to give

00:01:23.084 --> 00:01:27.077
advice that is actually
practical not makes me look cool.

00:01:27.077 --> 00:01:29.407
So that's why I love hustle.

00:01:29.407 --> 00:01:30.407
- Very nice.

00:01:31.743 --> 00:01:34.250
So the personal brand is something

00:01:34.250 --> 00:01:36.014
you speak on a lot it's something

00:01:36.014 --> 00:01:40.333
that social media has really
become possible for everyone.

00:01:40.333 --> 00:01:42.187
So what's the first step for someone

00:01:42.187 --> 00:01:44.066
to build that great personal brand?

00:01:44.066 --> 00:01:45.640
- To be self-aware of what they actually

00:01:45.640 --> 00:01:47.722
have to add to the conversation.

00:01:47.722 --> 00:01:49.691
You know being a personal brand for the

00:01:49.691 --> 00:01:51.707
sake of being a personal brand is usually

00:01:51.707 --> 00:01:54.646
the quickest way to not
be a personal brand.

00:01:54.646 --> 00:01:57.518
I think you have to
understand what you do,

00:01:57.518 --> 00:01:58.451
what you talk about.

00:01:58.451 --> 00:02:00.932
I mean I talk and talk and talk and talk

00:02:00.932 --> 00:02:02.287
and have for the last decade,

00:02:02.287 --> 00:02:04.002
but if you look carefully in a very narrow

00:02:04.002 --> 00:02:08.750
you know I haven't gone into
healthcare or geopolitical.

00:02:08.750 --> 00:02:11.513
You know I'm not talking
for the sake of talking

00:02:11.513 --> 00:02:14.832
or adding my two cents to
every pop culture situation.

00:02:14.832 --> 00:02:16.512
I talk about the things that I know.

00:02:16.512 --> 00:02:18.089
Communication in the modern world

00:02:18.089 --> 00:02:20.440
usually in a social network environment.

00:02:20.440 --> 00:02:23.391
More and more probably now in a voice

00:02:23.391 --> 00:02:25.785
environment as I become
fascinated with that platform.

00:02:25.785 --> 00:02:29.725
I think it's important to have a skill

00:02:29.725 --> 00:02:31.835
and then the next thing that's important

00:02:31.835 --> 00:02:33.391
is to understand how you communicate.

00:02:33.391 --> 00:02:37.136
You I'm guessing write
now clearly can write.

00:02:37.136 --> 00:02:39.220
You know other people can do audio,

00:02:39.220 --> 00:02:41.014
other people can do video I think

00:02:41.014 --> 00:02:43.784
the self-awareness of how
you're going to communicate

00:02:43.784 --> 00:02:45.263
in one of the three mediums of how

00:02:45.263 --> 00:02:48.182
people consume content
is massively important

00:02:48.182 --> 00:02:50.213
and so what are you
going to talk about and

00:02:50.213 --> 00:02:52.471
what's your best way of communicating that

00:02:52.471 --> 00:02:54.137
and once you understand that

00:02:54.137 --> 00:02:57.509
what is the current distribution
situations of those things.

00:02:57.509 --> 00:03:00.061
So if you're good at audio
you need to understand

00:03:00.061 --> 00:03:02.418
anchor you need to understand distribution

00:03:02.418 --> 00:03:05.802
of podcasts you need to
understand Alexa briefings.

00:03:05.802 --> 00:03:08.074
Written word you need to
understand what is happening

00:03:08.074 --> 00:03:10.466
on Facebook, and LinkedIn and Medium and

00:03:10.466 --> 00:03:13.036
contribution opportunities.

00:03:13.036 --> 00:03:14.957
And then video you need
to understand YouTube

00:03:14.957 --> 00:03:17.723
and Facebook and Vimeo which reminds me

00:03:17.723 --> 00:03:20.390
I still want a Vimeo movie ASAP.

00:03:22.280 --> 00:03:24.889
